<http://data.silknow.org/object/9df87378-37c2-34b0-b7b8-71d0a9c549cc>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "Ottoman Turkish Interior Textiles from the Aldrich Collection" , "A decorated napkin such as this one was a ceremonial object, placed on the lap of a guest at a meal but not generally used.  The drawn work, called muşabak, is a feature of 19th-century Turkish embroideries. This technique, seen here around each blue flower, creates tiny open squares in the ground of the cloth, a delicate addition to dense floral motifs." , "January 22 - July 17, 2016" ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/7ea1a31e-d419-3198-bbbc-b0b97de41221> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    "Exhibition" ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "A decorated napkin such as this one was a ceremonial object, placed on the lap of a guest at a meal but not generally used.  The drawn work, called muşabak, is a feature of 19th-century Turkish embroideries. This technique, seen here around each blue flower, creates tiny open squares in the ground of the cloth, a delicate addition to dense floral motifs." , "Ottoman Turkish Interior Textiles from the Aldrich Collection" , "January 22 - July 17, 2016" ;
        schema:contentUrl   <https://risdmuseum.org/exhibitions-events/exhibitions/ottoman-turkish-interior-textiles-aldrich-collection> .

